# Compressed in-memory swap for a 432MB board.
#
# WHY zram and not a swap file: the Raspbian kiosk swaps to the SD card, which
# makes memory pressure and I/O pressure the same problem -- the browser is
# competing with its own swap for the one slow card. zram costs RAM instead of
# I/O, and costs the card nothing.
#
# WHY 50 and not the recipe's default of 100: the zram device size is the
# UNCOMPRESSED capacity. At a typical 2:1 ratio a 100% device can consume half
# of physical RAM, which on 432MB leaves ~216MB for everything else. 50% gives
# roughly a 216MB device costing ~108MB when full -- a safety net rather than a
# second memory manager. The live kiosk's equivalent is a 99MB swap file that
# currently sits at 0 used.
ZRAM_SIZE_PERCENT=50

# WHY lzo-rle and not the recipe's default of lz4: this kernel has
# CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZO=y and CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP="lzo-rle" built in, while
# CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4=m. Asking zramctl for an algorithm behind a module that has
# not been loaded fails, and the failure is quiet -- the unit still looks
# healthy while there is no swap at all.
ZRAM_ALGORITHM=lzo-rle
